      "content": "hey, i've been looking into some stuff about the standard 440Hz tuning and its relation to the electrical grid frequencies. i've noticed that whenever i'm around high-frequency hums from the local substation, i feel this weird sense of fatigue and brain fog. is there any documented evidence of frequency modulation being used to influence human cognitive states or even just to keep people in a more lethargic state? it feels like it's more than just random noise.",
