      "content": "it just seems like we're only looking at the surface level. even if there isn't a \"peered-reviewed consensus,\" there's a massive amount of literature on how resonance and specific hertz levels affect biological systems. if someone wanted to induce a state of low-level stress or mental fatigue across a population, using existing infrastructure like the grid or standardized tuning would be the most efficient way to do it without anyone noticing.\n\ncould you do a deeper dive into the technical side of how \"harmonic resonance\" from power grids might actually overlap with the frequencies used in psychoacoustic studies to induce lethargy? like, is there a theoretical framework where the grid's baseline hum acts as a carrier wave for these kinds of frequencies?",
